{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n`python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity` (the operator-run parity harness) prints the following in a fresh worktree created by `make worktree`:\n\n```\nError: cannot list '<worktree>/.tickets-tracker': [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '<worktree>/.tickets-tracker'\n```\n\nThe run continues and makes model calls (see the 2026-11-09 correction comment). The error disappears once any `rebar` CLI command has run in that worktree, because the CLI creates the `.tickets-tracker` symlink.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed 2026-11-17 PST, origin/main 57d45053272)\n- Emitter: `rebar._ids._scan_tracker_root` (`src/rebar/_ids.py:268-272`) prints this line when `os.listdir(tracker_dir)` fails. In the harness it is reached through the code-review arm's deterministic finalize step: `finalize.py:356` → `bugfix_size_gate.apply_bugfix_size_gate` → `ticket_for_commit_message` (`src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py:151-164`), which resolves a commit trailer against `config.tracker_dir(repo_root)`. `repeat_fix.py:99` calls the same function.\n- Reproduced in a fresh worktree with no `.tickets-tracker`: `ticket_for_commit_message('fix\\n\\nrebar-ticket: d45f-229f-effe-4cf8\\n')` prints the exact line and returns `None`. So the error is not only cosmetic. In an unattached worktree the bug-fix size gate cannot resolve any ticket, and the code-review arm's repeat-fix/bugfix escalation differs from an attached worktree.\n- `--dry-run` and the pre-model part of every solver do not touch the tracker. Checked by running every corpus solver once with a runner that raises: no \"cannot list\" line.\n- Why the CLI does not hit it: the CLI dispatcher calls `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort()` (`src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:387`, defined at `src/rebar/_cli/_init.py:149-178`) before any command. In a linked worktree that function symlinks the main repo's tracker (`init_core` → `_init_via_symlink`, `src/rebar/_commands/init.py:541-598`). It never creates a first store and never raises. The `python -m` harnesses do not go through the dispatcher.\n- The sibling harness `python -m rebar.llm.evals.engine_comparison` has the same gap. Its `main` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py:441-494`) runs `rebar.llm.review_plan` and `rebar.show_ticket` (`:229`, `:254`) against the harness checkout's tracker.\n\n## Approach\nGive both operator harnesses the same store-mount step the CLI uses, at the point where a real run starts. Before any model call, after the `--dry-run` (and, in provider_parity, `--probe`) early returns, `main()` calls `rebar._cli._init.ensure_store_mounted_best_effort()`. Dry-run stays side-effect-free.\n- This reuses the CLI's own consent-free attach rules unchanged: it mounts an existing store by symlink or branch attach, never creates a first store, and never raises.\n- In a worktree that genuinely cannot attach, the existing per-call \"cannot list\" message still names the missing path.\n- No new config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py`: in `main` (`:583`), call `ensure_store_mounted_best_effort()` after the `--probe` and `--dry-run` returns and before `run_slot`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py`: in `main`, call it after the `--dry-run` return and before `run(...)`.\n- `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py` and `tests/unit/test_engine_comparison.py`: tests that the non-dry-run `main` calls the mount function before the run, and the dry-run path does not. Each monkeypatches `rebar._cli._init.ensure_store_mounted_best_effort` with a recorder and stubs the run (`run_slot` / `run`) to record call order.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: a non-dry-run `main` records the mount call before the first run call, for both harnesses.\n- Edge path: `--dry-run` records no mount call (both harnesses), and `--probe` records none (provider_parity).\n- Existing tests in both test modules still pass.\n- Manual check, recorded on this ticket: in a fresh `make worktree` checkout, `ticket_for_commit_message` reproduces the \"cannot list\" line. After a provider_parity `main` with `--limit 1` and a stubbed `run_slot` has run, `.tickets-tracker` is a symlink to the main store and `ticket_for_commit_message` resolves the trailer with no error line.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Both harnesses mount the existing tracker the way the CLI does before a real run, and not on `--dry-run`/`--probe`. Checked by the new unit tests.\n- [ ] In a fresh worktree, the manual check above shows the symlink created and no \"cannot list\" line, recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on the change."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794939557251608792,"uuid":"d9efbeaf-8ee0-41f4-ae5f-1260bcc03356"}